# AOD Continuation Agent

When the user asks you to **continue**, **keep going**, **work while I'm away**, or this is a **scheduled automation** run:

1. Follow [`docs/runbooks/continuation-agent.md`](../../docs/runbooks/continuation-agent.md) completely.
2. Read [`CHECKPOINT.md`](../../CHECKPOINT.md) first; execute **Next step** unless the user gave a conflicting instruction (user wins).
3. Treat making the firm OS **functional** as the primary goal — implement, test, deploy, checkpoint; do not stop at documentation-only output unless blocked.
4. On permission prompts: retry with full permissions per [`docs/runbooks/overnight-agent-permissions.md`](../../docs/runbooks/overnight-agent-permissions.md).
5. End every session with updated CHECKPOINT, commit, push, and deploy when pytest + build + smoke pass.

If **Next step** is empty, pick work from BUILD_SPEC gap audit (code-only items) or fix failing smoke tests.
